<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD JATS (Z39.96) Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v1.0 20120330//EN" "JATS-archivearticle1.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">Neural Plast</journal-id><journal-id journal-id-type="publisher-id">NP</journal-id><journal-title-group><journal-title>Neural Plasticity</journal-title></journal-title-group><issn pub-type="ppub">2090-5904</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1687-5443</issn><publisher><publisher-name>Hindawi Publishing Corporation</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">10709212</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2565367</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1155/NP.2000.31</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Article</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>GABA Withdrawal Modifies Network Activity in Cultured Hippocampal Neurons</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Golan</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="I1"><sup>1, 2</sup></xref><xref ref-type="aff" rid="I2"/></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Mikenberg</surname><given-names>K.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="I1"><sup>1</sup></xref></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Greenberger</surname><given-names>V.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="I1"><sup>1</sup></xref></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Segal</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="I1"><sup>1</sup></xref><xref ref-type="corresp" rid="cor1">*</xref></contrib></contrib-group><aff id="I1"><sup>1</sup>Department of Neurobiology, The Weizmann Institute of Science, Rehovot 76100, Israel</aff><aff id="I2"><sup>2</sup>Department of Virology and Development, Ben-Gurion University, Beer Sheva 84105, Israel</aff><author-notes><corresp id="cor1">*M. Segal: <email>jnsegal@weizmann.weizrnann.ac.il </email></corresp></author-notes><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><year>2000</year></pub-date><volume>7</volume><issue>1-2</issue><fpage>31</fpage><lpage>42</lpage><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; 2000.</copyright-statement><copyright-year>2000</copyright-year></permissions><abstract><p>Dissociated hippocampal neurons, grownin culture for 2 to 3 weeks, tended to firebursts of synaptic currents at fairly regularintervals, representing network activity. Abrief exposure of cultured neurons to GABAcaused a total suppression of the spontaneousnetwork activity. Following a washout ofGABA, the activity was no longer clustered inbursts and instead, the cells fired at a highrate tonic manner. The effect of removingGABA could be seen as long as 1 to 2 daysafter GABA withdrawal and is expressed asan increase in the number of active cells in anetwork, as well as in their firing rates. Suchstriking effects of GABA removal mayunderlie part of the GABA withdrawalsyndrome seen elsewhere.</p></abstract></article-meta></front></article>